## 9. AXI vs AXI4-Lite Terminology Clarification

Although vendor documentation often refers to an “AXI to APB Bridge,” practical implementations support **AXI4-Lite only**, as full AXI features such as bursts, IDs, and out-of-order transactions are incompatible with the APB protocol.

---

## 10. Conclusion

The AXI4-Lite to APB bridge is a critical SoC infrastructure component that enables high-performance AXI masters to access low-speed APB peripherals safely and efficiently. Each internal block resolves a specific protocol mismatch, ensuring correctness, scalability, and full compliance with AMBA standards.

